Lenscript — Privacy Policy
Last updated: November 9, 2026

The short version: Lenscript does not collect, transmit, or sell any of your data.
Your scripts stay on your device and — only if you turn it on — in your own
private iCloud. Takes you record stay on your device, inside the app, and go to
your Photos library only if you ask. Nothing is ever sent to the developer.

DEVELOPER
Lenscript is developed by Dzianis Milasheuski, an individual developer based in
Lithuania. Questions about this policy: info@porconova.com

WHAT I COLLECT
Nothing. Lenscript has no analytics, no advertising, no accounts, and no servers
that receive your data. There is no sign-up and no login. There are no
third-party SDKs and no trackers in the app. The app makes no network requests of
its own. I do not know who you are, what you read, or what you record.

The one exception is not mine to control and never contains your content: if you
have chosen in iOS Settings to share analytics and crash reports with app
developers, Apple may show me aggregated, anonymised statistics — how often the
app crashed, on which iOS versions. This comes from Apple, in aggregate, and
cannot be traced back to you or to anything you have written or recorded. You can
turn it off in Settings › Privacy & Security › Analytics & Improvements.

WHAT THE APP HOLDS
- Your scripts: the titles and text you type or paste, and where you stopped
  reading. They are kept in a local database inside the app's private container
  on your device. The app also adds two built-in example scripts that explain
  how it works; you can edit or delete them.
- Your takes: the recordings you choose to keep, with a short description of
  each (date, length, which script, how far you read). See "Recording" below.
- Your settings: text size, speed, countdown, mirror, text backdrop, which
  camera and microphone to record with, and similar preferences. The answers you
  give to the short questions when you first open the app are used only to set
  these defaults. All of it is kept on your device and is not synced.
None of it is indexed, counted, analysed, or shared.

The clipboard is read only when you tap the system Paste button: iOS hands the
text to the app at that moment. Before that, the app only checks whether the
clipboard holds any text at all, so that it can show the button as available; it
does not see what the text is.

IMPORTING SCRIPTS
You can bring in a script from a file you pick in the Files picker (PDF, Word,
RTF or plain text) or from the Share menu of another app. The text is read on
your device; the file is not uploaded anywhere, and the app keeps only the text,
as a new script. Only the file or text you choose is read, and only at that
moment. Text shared from another app is placed in a folder on your device that
only Lenscript and its Share extension can open, and becomes a script the next
time you open the app. Without Pro it waits on the Home screen until you get Pro
or remove it; a removed item is deleted. To tell you which of the two will
happen, the Share extension can see one thing besides the text you share:
whether Pro is active, a yes/no flag kept in that same on-device folder.

RECORDING VIDEO
Lenscript can record you while the words scroll — video with sound, video only,
or sound only — with your device's own camera and microphone, or with an
external camera or microphone you connect. Recording is optional and happens
only when you press the record button.
- While a take is being recorded and reviewed, the video is kept as a temporary
  file inside the app's private container.
- If you choose "Keep", the take is moved into the app's private container on
  your device and listed under its script. If you choose "Retake", close the
  take without keeping it, or leave the app, the temporary file is deleted.
  Leftover files are also deleted the next time the app starts.
- Kept takes are excluded from your device backup and are deleted when you
  delete the take, its script, or the app.
- A copy goes to your own Photos library only when you tap "To Photos" on a take,
  or if you turn on "Also save to Photos" in Settings. You can also share a take
  yourself with the system share sheet.
- Lenscript never uploads a video anywhere except, if you turn on "Sync takes",
  to your own iCloud (see below). What happens to a copy in your Photos
  library, or one you shared — including whether your Photos are synced to
  iCloud — is governed by your Photos and iCloud settings, not by this app.

PRIVATE iCLOUD SYNC (OPTIONAL, OFF BY DEFAULT, PART OF PRO)
If you turn on iCloud sync in Settings, Lenscript stores a copy of your scripts,
and a short description of each take (date, length, which script), in the
PRIVATE database of your own iCloud account, so your other devices signed in to
the same Apple Account show the same scripts. Settings are not synced.
Take files (video and sound) are synced only if you also turn on "Sync takes".
They are then stored in Lenscript's private folder in your own iCloud Drive and
count toward your iCloud storage. Turning it off keeps takes already in iCloud
there; new takes stay on the device.
- The data goes only to your iCloud. It does not pass through any server of mine,
  and I have no access to it.
- Apple stores it under your Apple Account, governed by Apple's privacy policy.
- Turning sync off stops the copying; your scripts stay on the device.
Sync also uses Apple's silent push notifications to learn that another device has
changed something. These carry no content of yours; they only wake the app.

PERMISSIONS THE APP MAY ASK FOR
- Camera — only in recording mode with video, to show you in the frame and record
  a take when you press record.
- Microphone — only in recording mode with sound. The free version records with
  the built-in microphone; with Pro you can pick another one (wired, USB or
  Bluetooth). The choice is kept on your device.
- Photos (add only) — only when you ask to add a take to your library.
  Lenscript asks for "add only" access: it cannot see, read, or change anything
  already in your Photos library.
- Notifications — only to remind you, one day before a free trial ends, that it is
  about to end. The reminder is scheduled and delivered locally by your device.
  Lenscript has no way to send you anything else, and no server that could.
You can use the prompter to read without granting any of these.

WHAT LEAVES YOUR DEVICE
Only what you explicitly send yourself:
- takes you choose to add to your own Photos library or share;
- your scripts and take descriptions, to your own iCloud, if you turn sync on;
- take files, to your own iCloud Drive, if you also turn on "Sync takes";
- an email you choose to write to support. The draft includes one line with the
  app version, device model, iOS version, whether Pro is active, and a random
  reference number that identifies nothing about you. You can delete that line
  before sending.
Nothing is uploaded automatically, and nothing is ever sent to me.

IF THE APP CANNOT OPEN ITS DATA
If the file that holds your scripts is ever damaged, Lenscript keeps the damaged
file on your device, next to a new empty one, so that it can be recovered. It is
not sent anywhere. If you write to support about it, I will explain how you can
share it with me yourself — only if you choose to.

PURCHASES
Lenscript Pro is sold through Apple's In-App Purchase. Apple, not the developer,
processes payment. I receive no personal or payment information. You can manage
or cancel a subscription in Settings › [Your Name] › Subscriptions on your
device.

YOUR RIGHTS
Because the app collects no personal information on the developer's side, there
is no developer-held data for you to access, correct, export, or delete.
- Any script can be deleted inside the app.
- Any take can be deleted inside the app. Copies you added to Photos are deleted
  there.
- Scripts and takes in your iCloud can be removed by deleting them in the app
  while sync is on, by signing out of iCloud, or from your iCloud storage in
  iOS Settings.
- Deleting the app removes the on-device copy.
- An active subscription can be cancelled in your Apple Account subscriptions.

INFORMATION ABOUT OTHER PEOPLE
If other people appear or can be heard in a video you record, that video is kept
only on your device and wherever you choose to put it. It is never transmitted to
the developer or to any third party. You are responsible for recording other
people only where you are allowed to.

CHILDREN
Lenscript is not directed at children under the age of 13 and does not knowingly
collect any data from children.

REGULATORY NOTES
The app is designed so that no directly identifying personal information (name,
email, IP address, advertising identifier, account ID) is collected by the
developer or by any third party the developer uses. There are no third-party
SDKs, no trackers, and no data brokers. Where Apple acts as a processor for
purchases and for iCloud, those activities are governed by Apple's own privacy
policy. Because no personal data is collected or processed by the developer,
there is no data controller obligation to transfer data internationally, and no
data retention period to declare on the developer's side. What you write and
record is created, stored and erased entirely by you; the developer is neither
its controller nor its processor and cannot reach it.

